          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            Classically, the
            %strong fundamental theorem of algebra
            states that
          %ul
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+function"} polynomial function
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/root"} root
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
          %p
            Since every non-zero polynomial could be made a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monic+polynomial"} monic polynomial
            by dividing by the leading coefficient, it could also be expressed as
          %ul
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrally+closed+field"} integrally closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monic+polynomial"} monic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+function"} polynomial function
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/root"} root
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
          %p
            Many proofs of this theorem are known (see the
            %a{:href => "#References"} references
            below); some use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analysis"} complex analysis
            (the reciprocal of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+function"} polynomial function
            cannot be bounded), some use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            (the degree of a map is invariant with respect to homotopy), and some use advanced calculus (polynomial functions on the complex numbers are
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"} open mappings
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+number"} Dedekind complete
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+field"} archimedean
          %h2#algebraic_proof_via_real_closed_fields Algebraic proof via real closed fields
          %p
            Despite its name, the fundamental theorem of algebra makes reference to a concept from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            (the field of complex numbers). However, the analytic part may be reduced to a minimum: that the field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+closed+field"} real closed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+value+theorem"} intermediate value theorem
          %p
            The rest of the proof is algebraic and, unlike the other proof methods, applies to all
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+closed+field"} real closed field
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+Artin"} Emil Artin
          %p
            We recall that a
            %em real closed field
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+field"} ordered field
            such that every positive element has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 + 1
            cannot have any root in a real closed field — or in fact in any ordered field, since we always have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2\ge 0
            and hence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2+1 \ge 1
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is real closed, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msqrt
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = F[\sqrt{-1}]
              is algebraically closed.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We must show that any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+polynomial"} irreducible polynomial
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              of degree greater than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              with coefficients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              has a root in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              has characteristic
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect field
            %p
              Thus the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+field"} splitting field
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+extension"} Galois extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"} Galois group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(2)
              is the
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/class+equation#sylow_theorems"} Sylow 2-group
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %span.newWikiWord
                fixed field
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/fixed+field"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(2)
              is an odd degree extension of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in E
              must then have an irreducible polynomial function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \in F[x]
              of odd degree. But since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is real closed,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              has a root in
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \deg(q) = 1
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = F
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = G(2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|G|} \gt 1
              since the splitting field contains
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p
              So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/primary+group"} primary group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              = succeed "-group" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center"} center
              (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/show/class+equation#pgroup"} here
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solvable+group"} solvable
              by an inductive argument. Therefore the extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L/F
              arises from a tower of non-trivial
              = succeed "s" do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  quadratic extension
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/quadratic+extension"} ?
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi …
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subseteq L_1 \subseteq \ldots \subseteq L_n = L
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+formula"} quadratic formula
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_1
              arises by adjoining roots to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              of a polynomial function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mi a
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 + a x + b
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi a
                        %mo ±
                        %msqrt
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi a
                              %mn 2
                            %mo −
                            %mn 4
                            %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{-a \pm \sqrt{a^2 - 4b}}{2},
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %mn 4
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^2 - 4b
              is negative. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is real closed, the positive element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 4
                    %mi b
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4b - a^2
              has a square root in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo =
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msqrt
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = F[\sqrt{-1}]
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_1 = K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              has no nontrivial quadratic extensions by the lemma that follows, so in fact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_1 = L_n = K
              and the theorem is proved.
          #sqrt.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Every element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msqrt
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = F[\sqrt{-1}]
              has a square root in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The proof is most easily apprehended by analogy with polar coordinate representations of complex numbers and half-angle formulas, where a square root of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r e^{i\theta}
              is given by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi θ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^{1/2}e^{i\theta /2}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              be a fixed square root of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + b i
              be an arbitrary element of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b \in F
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi y
                      %mi i
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x + y i)^2 = a + b i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in F
              that solve
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mn 2
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 - y^2 = a, \qquad 2x y = b
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^2 + b^2
              has a square root in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b)
              is on the unit circle:
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^2 + b^2 = 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              if need be, we may assume
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq a \leq 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -y
              if need be, we may assume
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \geq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \geq 0
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 = \frac{1+a}{2}, \qquad y^2 = \frac{1-a}{2},
            %p
              we obtain a solution (since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi y
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 - y^2 = a
              and
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4 x^2 y^2 = b^2
          %h2#classical_fta_via_advanced_calculus Classical FTA via advanced calculus
          %p
            As noted above, many proofs of the fundamental theorem are known. The following proof, ultimately rooted in the fact that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+mappings"} polynomial mappings
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+mappings"} open mappings
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"} Todd Trimble
            = succeed "." do
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{C}
            be a nonconstant polynomial mapping, and suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            has no zero.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infimum"} infimum
                of values
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|f(z)|}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_1, z_2, z_3, \ldots
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi z
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo →
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|f(z_n)|} \to s
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mrow
                            %mi z
                            %mo →
                            %mn ∞
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_{z \to \infty} f(z) = \infty
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_n
                must be bounded; by the Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem it has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} subsequence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_{n_k}
                that converges to some point
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|f(z_{n_k})|}
                converges to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
